From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:35:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(blocks): preserve native occlusion with MoreCulling

MoreCulling 1.9.0-beta.1 derives full cached bottom faces from the converted
bed model even though the live block state has empty occlusion. With the
pinned 26.3 graphics modpack and BDS 1.26.60.6/protocol 2225, those faces
hide the stone floor beneath the bed. Disabling its block-state culling
and rebuilding both affected sections restores the floor. Re-enabling
the setting reproduces the hole without changing the final block states.

Adapt MoreCulling's face query to the live block-state occlusion while
accepted, protocol-bound Bedrock rendering metadata owns the world.
This uses the same native face hooks as ordinary terrain and custom
carrier blocks on direct and ViaProxy connections. Keep the host cache
intact so Java sessions and resource removal retain their own behavior.

Gate the optional mixin on MoreCulling presence and require no mod API
dependency. Preserve the native solid-neighbor faces rather than disabling
the mod or its culling globally. Regression coverage exercises bed halves,
solid neighbors, and entry/exit through accepted metadata. Other culling
shapes, shield poses, and full third-party graphics parity remain open.
